WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.501
-Our next guest
is a very talented actor

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.834
you know from shows
such as "Private Practice"

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:07.133
and films like "Rent"
and "The Best Man" franchise.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.701
He stars in "All American,"

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.534
which airs Monday nights
on the CW.

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:11.701
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:13.601
-My dad is gone.

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:16.467
-♪ Gone, gone ♪

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.667
-Anyway, I'm sorry this message
got way too long.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:21.434
But, uh, like you, I had
some things I needed to say,

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:24.267
and, uh --
and I'm glad I did it.

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:29.367
Um, I love you, Spencer James,
and I always will.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:33.400
You are my all American.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.868
So, I know you said
you needed some time.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:40.167
Um, I'm here
whenever you're ready

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:43.634
uh, because, you know,
you and me,

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.567
we got all the time
in the world.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:48.667
-Please welcome back to the show
Taye Diggs, everybody.

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.667 --> 00:01:00.734
♪♪

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:03.667
♪♪

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.701
-All right, thank you, sir.
-Welcome back!

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:08.033
-Yes.
Real quick.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.934
Real quick.
Have y'all seen his stand-up?

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:12.634
-Okay.
-His -- yo.

00:01:12.634 --> 00:01:15.067
-Very kind.
-It is so good, I saw it twice.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.067
-Oh, wow!
-I saw it twice.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.467
And I don't see
white boys twice.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:18.467
I saw it twice,
so it's good stuff.

00:01:18.467 --> 00:01:19.367
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:21.467
Oh, my God.
Double white boy.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.834
-Yeah, man.
-That is -- oh!

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:25.133
This is --
Thank you for saying that.

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:26.934
That is very flattering.
-I was very impressed.

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.868
-So this is, you know,
for people who aren't

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:30.968
engaged with the show
and haven't seen it,

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:32.467
this was the end
of your character's arc.

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.634
This is five years
playing a football coach.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.901
-Yes, yes, yes.
-A very shocking ending

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:38.734
to your character arc.
-Yes, yes, yes.

00:01:38.734 --> 00:01:40.200
-Did you enjoy playing
a high school football coach?

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:42.267
-I had a ball.
I had a ball.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.934
It really helped --
I have a 13-year-old son

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:48.868
who is an athlete,
so I was able to kind of use

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:52.501
what I was doing at work with my
son at his games and whatnot.

00:01:52.501 --> 00:01:56.133
So, it was a life-changing role.
I'm very thankful.

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:58.834
-When you were 13, were you
athletic or were you..,?

00:01:58.834 --> 00:02:01.400
-I was athletic.
I wasn't an athlete.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.534
-Gotcha.
-Yes.

00:02:02.534 --> 00:02:04.534
-Because you already knew,
at that point,

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.200
theater was your path?
-Yes, yes.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.400
Because I was not an athlete.
-Gotcha.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.501
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:12.567
But we have a photo.
-Yes.

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:14.767
-You tell us what age
this is of Taye Diggs.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.167
-I think that's the age nerd.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:19.367
-Yeah.
-That's what I've heard, yeah.

00:02:19.367 --> 00:02:21.167
-I would say, like,
there's nobody --

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.634
If you use one of those apps
that guesses what you're gonna

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:27.167
look like as an adult, no one
guessed Taye Diggs on this.

00:02:27.167 --> 00:02:28.300
[ Laughter ]
-No.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.133
-This never led to that.

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.567
And any A.I. ever would have
predicted that.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:36.934
-That's why I was
into music theater, yes.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.501
-So, you went to Syracuse,

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:40.033
and you started doing
music theater there.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.734
-Yes.
And then -- is it,

00:02:42.734 --> 00:02:45.033
You get a job at Tokyo Disney.

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:46.801
-Okay, we're going there.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:49.067
[ Laughter ]
So is that right out of college?

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:51.467
-That was --
Actually, it's weird.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:54.834
I -- I had already done
a Broadway show.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:57.067
-Okay.
-And then a friend of mine

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:59.400
had come back from Tokyo Disney

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.801
and said
that he had a great time.

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.934
I hadn't traveled.
So I said, "I'm gonna take

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:05.367
some time off and go over there
and have an experience."

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:06.934
And it was amazing.
It was amazing.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:09.601
Then I came back,
and then I got "Rent," so...

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.701
-Which is the life-changer.
-Yes, yes.

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:13.834
Game-changer,
yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
All right.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:19.267
-Obviously, you know, "Rent"
is an incredible accomplishment.

00:03:19.267 --> 00:03:21.067
What were you doing
at Tokyo Disney?

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:25.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.300
-We want to go back?
Okay.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.701
Uh, I was --
I was the host of a show

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:33.601
called "Sebastian's
Caribbean Carnival."

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:34.801
-Okay.
-Yes.

00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.033
-Sebastian from
"The Little Mermaid."

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.334
-Yes, "The Little Mermaid."
-Yep.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:40.601
-So, it was me,
and it was the crab.

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:42.167
[ Laughter ]
And then all of the --

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.467
And then,
Mickey and Minnie were there,

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:45.367
which was cool.
-Well, that's a coincidence.

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:46.968
-Yeah, yeah, it was great.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:48.334
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:51.934
And I sang,
and I had bananas on my arms.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.734
-Uh-huh.
-And a straw hat.

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:56.033
And it was --
it was tons of fun.

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:57.133
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.133 --> 00:03:59.334
How many shows a day
were you doing?

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:02.734
-It was, um...

00:04:02.734 --> 00:04:04.567
five.
Five shows a day.

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:07.300
-That does not seem like --
you were earning it.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:09.801
-100%.
100%. Yeah.

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:13.434
And we made a good wage,
but I learned the language

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:15.501
and went to the temples.

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:17.000
I climbed Mount Fuji,
which was cool.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.300
-Well, there you go.
That's an incredible experience.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.200
-It was great.
-And now, you know, I do think,

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.501
you know, it's really important

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:22.934
for actors to do experiences
like that.

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.234
-Yes.
-Because I'm assuming "Rent"

00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:26.367
was also incredibly taxing,
but it probably helps

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:29.133
to do something --
-Oh, 100%.

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:31.601
Yeah,
soap operas and theme park.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:34.801
Nothing is more difficult.
-Yeah, I believe it.

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:37.734
-I was on a soap opera,
and the amount of material

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:40.367
you have to learn in a day
is ridiculous.

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:42.167
So, it was a muscle
that I developed

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:45.200
and used later on in life.
-So, post-"Rent" --

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.868
obviously is
a Broadway sensation --

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:50.434
and then your first film
is "Stella,"

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:51.501
"How Stella
Got Her Groove Back."

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:52.834
-Yes, yes.
-Which I just saw.

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:54.033
It was Valentine's Day
this week.

00:04:54.033 --> 00:04:55.701
It was on a list of like --
-Was it?

00:04:55.701 --> 00:04:57.000
-The best 40.
I saw it.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.467
One of the best 40 romantic
comedies of all time.

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.167
-For real?
-Yeah.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:03.701
-Yes!
I always wanted to make a list.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:04.834
-There you go --
you made the list.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:06.767
-Yes!
I made the list.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:08.934
-And so that --
What was that transition like?

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.767
Because now you've done
soap operas, theme parks,

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:13.334
you've done Broadway.

00:05:13.334 --> 00:05:16.767
Is film easy or hard?
-It was --

00:05:16.767 --> 00:05:18.567
Well, let me --
I was very confident

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:20.434
leaving college, right?

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:23.501
I felt like I knew, you know,
what I was supposed to do.

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:26.067
So, I moved
straight to New York,

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:30.934
and my first job
was a host at Pizzeria Uno.

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:33.567
And my other two hostesses,
when we were talking about

00:05:33.567 --> 00:05:35.334
what we did
and what we were gonna do,

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.467
I said I was gonna be an actor,
and they scoffed.

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:38.934
And I said,
"You think I'm playing.

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:41.467
Give me a year,
and I'll either be in a movie,

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:44.067
have my own TV show,
or be on Broadway."

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:46.467
And in six months,
I was on Broadway.

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:50.968
So, when "Stella" came,
I was like, "Okay, cool.

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:52.601
I wish it had been a little
earlier, but..."

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:54.300
You know what I mean?
So, I was ready.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.834
-I bet those two people
you worked with

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:57.868
were happy when it happened.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.868 --> 00:06:00.200
They were like, if he gets
two out of three in a year,

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:01.734
we're never gonna
want to talk to him again.

00:06:01.734 --> 00:06:04.234
-I told them.
Seven pieces.

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:06.501
-And was that a film while you
were making it, were you like,

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:08.334
"Oh, this is gonna be something
that people are gonna

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:09.567
respond to,
that's going to endure?"

00:06:09.567 --> 00:06:10.901
-I'm so embarrassed.

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:14.567
I didn't know how
the whole industry worked.

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:16.634
So, you know,
I grew up reading "Us" magazine

00:06:16.634 --> 00:06:18.968
and seeing the paparazzi.

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:21.901
The first day I came home
from the movie,

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:24.033
I thought that there
were gonna be television cameras

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:26.734
in my apartment.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.734 --> 00:06:29.200
And I was like,
"Where is everybody?"

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:32.067
I didn't realize that the movie
hadn't even come out.

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:33.968
-You had a voicemail
from your Pizzeria Uno

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:35.200
being like,
"You're late for your shift."

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.367
[ Laughter ]
-Exactly!

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:38.968
Exactly!
Nobody knew!

00:06:38.968 --> 00:06:41.467
Nobody knew.
-Another film you made,

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.267
"The Best Man,"
which became a franchise

00:06:43.267 --> 00:06:44.901
and now a show
over on Peacock...

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:46.234
[ Applause ]
-Thank you, guys. Thank you.

00:06:46.234 --> 00:06:48.067
Yeah.
-And now that also must be

00:06:48.067 --> 00:06:50.000
a special thing not only to make
something that people

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.901
still care about,
but to be able to keep

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:53.334
going back and doing it
with the same group of people.

00:06:53.334 --> 00:06:55.834
-Yeah.
Yeah, I feel very, very lucky.

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:59.234
These people, the actors
and actresses from "Best Man,"

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:00.434
they're family.

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:02.400
We all kind of started
at the same time.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.901
And to be able to grow
with each other on --

00:07:05.901 --> 00:07:09.334
in such a piece is great.

00:07:09.334 --> 00:07:11.167
-Wow.
-We've all seen each other

00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:14.367
go through, you know, trials
and tribulation and breakups

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:17.467
and families and divorces.

00:07:17.467 --> 00:07:20.000
And it's really great.
It's comforting.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.968
-Yeah, it also is a nice
parallel, I guess,

00:07:22.968 --> 00:07:25.367
because, of course, that's
what's happening in those films.

00:07:25.367 --> 00:07:26.868
You're just watching them
grow up, characters.

00:07:26.868 --> 00:07:28.100
And knowing the same
is happening in real life.

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:29.334
-So it was easy.
It was easy.

00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:32.667
We all thought it would be
the last, but it's good.

00:07:32.667 --> 00:07:34.534
I watched it, and it's good.

00:07:34.534 --> 00:07:36.434
And so who knows?
-Yeah.

00:07:36.434 --> 00:07:38.133
Well, there's no reason
to close the door.

00:07:38.133 --> 00:07:39.701
Hey, what a delight
to have you back here.

00:07:39.701 --> 00:07:41.267
-My man.
-Really, really, really

00:07:41.267 --> 00:07:42.501
always appreciate seeing you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:42.501 --> 00:07:45.033
-Thank you, sir.
-Taye Diggs, everybody!

00:07:45.033 --> 00:07:47.300
"All American" airs
Monday nights at 8:00 p.m.

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.133
on the CW. Right back
with more "Late Night."

